I am out on the street again.
Everything is finally in place.
It is time for a little celebration.
I see a little bakery on the corner.
I go inside.
It smells lovely.
A baker stands behind the counter.
"Hello," the baker says.
"Hello," I reply.
I point to a pastry behind the glass.
"I would like a cinnamon pastry," I say.
"Yes, of course," he says.
"What does it cost?" I ask.
"It costs twenty-five kroner," the baker replies.
I have my wallet in my bag.
I take out my debit card.
I pay for my cinnamon pastry.
The baker gives me a small bag.
Now I have a cinnamon pastry for my little celebration.
